course: dictionary
lesson: 12958
title: Getting rid of waste
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Every living thing makes waste inside its body. To excrete means to get rid of that waste so it does not build up and harm you. «Your kidneys excrete urine, which is wee.» Here excrete is the action, and urine is the waste.
explain: Look at the words around excrete to work out its meaning. «Your lungs excrete carbon dioxide when you breathe out.» «Your skin excretes sweat when you get hot.» Both are examples of excretion, the noun for the whole process.
explain: Plants do it too. «Plants excrete waste gases through their leaves.» Check your idea by swapping in "get rid of" for excrete. If the sentence still makes sense, you have the right meaning.
fact: Excrete is a verb. Its forms are excrete, excretes, excreted and excreting.
fact: Excretion is the noun. It means the process of getting rid of waste.
fact: Excretion is one of the seven life processes, remembered as MRS GREN.
fact: The kidneys excrete urine, the lungs excrete carbon dioxide, and the skin excretes sweat.
fact: «Excreted» is the past form, so it is used for waste that has already been got rid of.
exercise: «Your kidneys excrete urine.» What does excrete mean here? | *To get rid of waste | To breathe in air | To eat food | To grow taller
exercise: «Plants excrete waste gases through their leaves.» Where do plants excrete waste gases? | *Through their leaves | Through their flowers | Through their stems in the soil | Through their roots
exercise: Which of these is excreted by the lungs? | *Carbon dioxide | Food | Oxygen
test: What does the skin excrete when you get hot? | Food | *Sweat | Air | Urine
test: Which word is the noun for the process of getting rid of waste? | Excrete | Excreting | Excretes | *Excretion
exam: Which body part excretes urine? | Lungs | Skin | *Kidneys | Heart
